{
  "_comment": [
    "One real fleet's shape, with invented names, so the harness tests what a",
    "fleet actually looks like rather than a convenient five-host toy. Twice in",
    "one session a harness that did not match let a real bug through: a",
    "nineteen-host tally is 70px wider than a five-host one, which is exactly",
    "the margin the toolbar had.",
    "",
    "The names are made up and the addresses are absent, because the harness",
    "never connects to anything and nobody's infrastructure belongs in a public",
    "tree. The *shape* is what these tests depend on: the count, the core",
    "counts, the physical/virtual mix, the one Windows host, the group names.",
    "Keep those honest when the fleet changes.",
    "",
    "Two properties of the names themselves are load-bearing, and both were",
    "learned by breaking them. Length, because a host name is drawn on a card",
    "and counted into the toolbar tally the layout suite measures. Alphabetical",
    "order, because filter.js falls back to the name as a sort tiebreak and",
    "`equal_values_fall_back_to_cpu_then_memory` asserts the result."
  ],
